<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Why builders switch from Procore (or skip it entirely)</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 space-y-3 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Cost:</strong> Procore's pricing is tied to your annual construction volume. For a small or mid-size builder, that can mean tens of thousands per year for features you may never touch.</li>
    <li><strong>Complexity:</strong> Procore is designed for very large GCs with dedicated IT and admin staff. Most small builders only need budgets, schedules, POs, and invoices.</li>
    <li><strong>Onboarding time:</strong> Enterprise tools can take weeks of training. SSI is designed to get a project set up in under an hour.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-collaborator fees:</strong> If you bring trades or owners into the platform, costs multiply quickly. With SSI, any other SSI subscriber can collaborate on your projects at no extra cost.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">When Procore <em>is</em> still the right fit</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">We won't pretend SSI is for everyone. Procore is genuinely the better choice if you:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
    <li>Run a large general contracting firm with dedicated IT, finance, and project controls teams.</li>
    <li>Need deep BIM coordination, large-scale RFIs/submittals workflows, or enterprise integrations (ERP, accounting suites, drawing management).</li>
    <li>Have annual construction volumes in the high tens of millions or more.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">If that's not you, SSI Construction Manager is built specifically for the rest of the industry — and at a price that won't eat your margin.</p>
</section>

